      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "International status",
          "heading": "France establishes its position alongside rugby's traditional southern hemisphere giants",
          "body": "France is increasingly viewed as a permanent third superpower in world rugby, challenging the historical dominance of the All Blacks and the Springboks. Following a strong showing in the Nations Championship and a convincing 42-15 victory over Japan in Round 3, the side has solidified its standing. With two wins from three matches, France currently sits third on the log with a points difference of +41, maintaining consistent pressure on the top two as they prepare for Fiji."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks maintain World Rugby ranking lead over New Zealand",
          "body": "Scotland U20 scrum-half Hector Patterson weighs international eligibility."
