      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Scrum concerns",
          "heading": "Eddie O’Sullivan highlights Springbok scrum dominance as challenge for Andy Farrell",
          "body": "Following Leinster’s recent difficulties in Durban, former Ireland coach Eddie O’Sullivan has warned that South Africa’s set-piece power presents a significant challenge for Andy Farrell’s side. O’Sullivan noted that the Springbok scrum is currently dominating international rugby, describing the physical pressure as a problem for all nations rather than an isolated Irish issue. With Ireland scheduled to host the world champions in November, concern persists after the Irish front-row previously conceded multiple penalties against the South African pack."
        },
        {
